contracts.py, geometry.py and parts of bridge.py are a modified port of files of ASPIRE
(https://github.com/NVlabs/ASPIRE), at commit fa00f0ef2bc1d91d594b9aa502c22133c9f538f7: src/cap_harness/contracts.py,
errors.py, protocols.py, geometry.py, api.py and runtime.py. ASPIRE is under the Apache License 2.0
(https://github.com/NVlabs/ASPIRE/blob/fa00f0ef2bc1d91d594b9aa502c22133c9f538f7/LICENSE).

Positronic changed the port:

- It takes the joint count of an arm from the rig's state, and the embodiment name from a setting.
- It keeps two perception types, segmentations and point clouds. It drops the other perception types and the
  planning types.
- Its segmentation provider protocol has text prompts only.
- geometry.py keeps mask_to_point_cloud only. It refuses a view with no depth, no intrinsics or no pose in the
  target frame.
- A camera observation can hold RGB without depth, intrinsics or pose. It refuses a depth of another size than its
  image.

